Subagents:- [DONE]
===========
=>Subagents give you three main benefits:
	=>They break work into focused pieces, letting each subagent concentrate on a specific task.
	=>They keep your main context window clean by isolating all the intermediate work.
	=>They bring back just the information you need as a concise summary.	


=>Subagents are specialized assistants that Claude Code can delegate tasks to.
=>runs in its own conversation context window, does its work, and returns a summary to the main thread.

=>Why Subagents Matter?
	=> Every time you chat with Claude Code, you're adding to the main context window. 
	=>Every tool call, every file read, every search result gets stored there. 
	=>That space is finite, and once it fills up, Claude starts losing track of earlier parts 
	  of the conversation.

=>The subagent receives two things:
	=>A custom system prompt from your configuration file that defines the subagent's role and behavior.
	=>A task description written by the parent agent based on what you asked for.

=> Built-in Subagents
	=>General purpose subagent -- for multi-step tasks that require both exploration and action.
	=>Explore -- for fast searching and navigation of codebases.
	=>Plan -- used during plan mode for research and analysis of your codebase before presenting a plan.

=>Custom Subagents
	=>it can be a code reviewer, a test writer, a documentation generator, or anything else you need.



=>/agent:-
	=> crate new agent (name, desc, tools)
	=>bykon y2ma user-level y2ma project-level
	=>w recommended 5aly el AI hoa eli y3ml generate ll hagat de.
	=>Customizing Tools: 
		Read-only tools
		Edit tools
		Execution tools
		MCP tools
		Other tools
	=>Choosing a Model and Color:
		Haiku -- best for fast, lightweight tasks
		Sonnet -- a good middle ground between speed and depth
		Opus -- best for complex analysis
		Inherit -- uses whatever model your main conversation is running
	=>w kman t2dr t8er lon el agent w t5tar lon mo3en
	=>system prompt: ay text mwgod b2a t7t w hoa dh eli bymyz subagent 3n el tany.
	=>path for it on your machine: .claude/agents/your-agent-name.md
	=>lw 3awz claude hoa eli ydy el task ll sub-agent automatically w kda ektb f el desc kelmt
          "proactively" such as description: Proactively suggest running this agent after major code 
	  changes...
	=>34an t5ly el sub-agent y run automatic b2a, ektb desc kois 34an dh bysa3d el system prompt kman.
	=>Defining an Output Format:
		=>lazm t7dd eh el output w dh by3rfo eno khalas it's done w gablk el result.



=>How to use?
	=>by asking Claude directly or by typing @agent code-quality-reviewer in your message.
	=>


=>

