Agent Skills:- [DONE]
==============
https://github.com/anthropics/skills
https://claude.com/blog/equipping-agents-for-the-real-world-with-agent-skills

https://github.com/mhattingpete/claude-skills-marketplace/tree/main
https://github.com/emarco177/claude-code-crash-course/tree/project/skills

=> de skills bt3mlha install mn /plugin w t3ml install lyha w tbd2 tst5dmha.
=>zy msln el skill bta3t git pushing
	=>https://github.com/mhattingpete/claude-skills-marketplace/tree/main/engineering-workflow-plugin/skills/git-pushing
	=>3ml nfs el folder structure t7t .claude/skills/...
	=>5d el hagat copy past blzbt w bs kda. 

------

=>el skills bt run automatic mn 8er ma a3mlha call
=>lw 3andy aktr mn skill b nfs el esm  claude hy load men fyhom? fe priority
	Enterprise — managed settings, highest priority
	Personal — your home directory (~/.claude/skills)
	Project — the .claude/skills directory inside a repository
	Plugins — installed plugins, lowest priority

	=>Enterprise (eli hoa bta3 claude nfso b2a)
	=>Personal (eli hoa f el home directory bta3k enta bs)
	=>Project (eli hoa goa planradar bs)
	=>Plugins (eli hoa goa el project f .calude-plugins/skills)


=>tb3n e7na bnst5dm el skills enna 7aten name w description w khalas bs f advanced settings momkn nst5dmha
	=>allowed-tools: de optional w bt5lek t7dd eh el tools el msmo7a w hoa byst5dm el skills de
	=>model: anhy model eli ysht8l m3 el skill de
	=>Progressive disclosure: keep SKILL.md under 500 lines and link to supporting files 
	  (references, scripts, assets) that Claude reads only when needed.
	=>Scripts execute without loading their contents into context — only the output consumes tokens,
	  keeping context efficient.
	=>lw l2et el skill msh by7slha call rag3 el keywords eli f el desc w eli enta btktbha.


=>Sharing Skills
	=>Project skills in .claude/skills are shared automatically through Git 
	=>Plugins let you distribute skills across repositories via marketplaces 
	=>Enterprise managed settings deploy skills organization-wide with the highest priority, 
	  ideal for mandatory standards and compliance.
	=>Subagents don't automatically see your skills — you must explicitly list skills in a 
	  custom agent's frontmatter skills field.
	=>Built-in agents (Explorer, Plan, Verify) can't access skills at all — only 
	  custom subagents defined in .claude/agents can.
	=>


=>el sub-agents msh byshofo el skills bta3tk lma btdehom task, eli hyshof el skills bta3tk el sub-agents
  eli enta 3mltlhom create w lazm t list el skills de gwahom w tt2kd enha mwgoda.

=>lma tkon 3awz t3ml debug: claude --debug

=>lma ykon f moshkla f el skill, msh sh8ala aw darba aw ay haga fa fe et7mal mn dol
	=>Start with the skills validator tool — it catches structural problems before 
	  you spend time debugging other things.
		-uv tool install skills-ref
		-skills-ref validate ~/.claude/skills/backend-review

	=>If a skill doesn't trigger, the cause is almost always the description — 
	  add trigger phrases that match how you actually phrase requests.
	=>If a skill doesn't load, check that SKILL.md is inside a named directory 
	  (not at the skills root) and the file name is exactly SKILL.md
	=>If the wrong skill gets used, your descriptions are too similar — make them more distinct
	=>For runtime errors, check dependencies, file permissions (chmod +x), and 
	  path separators (use forward slashes everywhere).
	=>Plugin Skills Not Appearing: Clear the cache, restart Claude Code, and reinstall.

=>Quick Troubleshooting Checklist:
	=>Not triggering? Improve your description and add trigger phrases.
	=>Not loading? Check your path, file name, and YAML syntax.
	=>Wrong skill used? Make descriptions more distinct from each other.
	=>Being shadowed? Check the priority hierarchy and rename if needed.
	=>Plugin skills missing? Clear cache and reinstall.
	=>Runtime failure? Check dependencies, permissions, and paths.


=>Ask Claude what happened if I called skill manually? Is it okay or not?
	=>disable-model-invocation: true: The skill can only be invoked manually via /skill-name, and 
	  Claude won't trigger it on its own. Best for skills with side effects, 
	  like commands that create or update Jira tickets or Confluence pages.
	=>user-invocable: false: The opposite. The skill is hidden from the / menu, and only Claude 
	  can load it automatically. Best for background knowledge or 
	  reference material rather than actions.


=>How to use? 
	=>by7slha detect mn el msg bta3tk 34an by3mlha match m3 el name w el des
	=>aw enta t3ml /skill-name b nfsk w tkon sayb el default mood mt8yrosh 
	  34an ymshy 3 el template bta3tk.
	=>path for it on your machine: .claude/skills 

